codex
The supplied m88k example is safe because `w` is masked to 0–31 and the left operand is cast to `uint32_t`. The `w == 0` branch supplies the all-ones mask; it is not what makes shifting by 31 safe. I also found the same unsigned idiom in three nearby sites.

exec
"C:\\WINDOWS\\System32\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe" -Command "rg -n -- '\\(uint32_t\\)1\\s*<<|1[Uu](?:[Ll]{1,2})?\\s*<<|1[Ll]{1,2}[Uu]\\s*<<' GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices -g '*.c' -g '*.h'" in C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL
